### Capability Model & Sandboxing
  - Process-local tokens. Landlock is a real Linux jail under `&SysCap` (`oo_landlock_restrict`). Empty allowlists fail closed. Proved `OK: LANDLOCK_JAIL` on this host.
  - POSIX `setrlimit` is product under `&SysCap` (AS / NOFILE / CPU). Zero quotas fail closed.
  - `spawn` / `wait` / `kill` are real. Child env is filtered (`OODA_`/`OO_` and `PATH`).
  - Hostile probes: `env_get` denies host keys; zero `FsWriteCap` exits; child drops `HOST_SECRET`; attenuate forged parent differs. Lock: `scripts/hostile_cap_probe_smoke.oo`.
  - `process_exec` is a shell line and a secret sink.
  - `GpuCap` CPU/noop launch is product. `emit_ptx` writes real kernel PTX text (`add.s64`); device GPU dispatch is residual. Not CUDA, not a device launch.
  - Hierarchical HMAC attenuation, kernel object-cap seals, and measured isolate (hash of payload+token+domain) are product. Not SGX/TDX/SEV hardware enclaves. HMAC-SHA256 of a cap payload string is product.
  - Bump arenas (`arena_create`/`alloc`/`reset`) under AllocCap, `&ArenaCap` as its own token, and `actor_restart` under ThreadCap are product.

